Replaced the linear scan with a binary search over the profile’s message table, which is ordered by message number, cutting lookup cost from O(MESGS) to O(log MESGS). This preserves the same returned pointer for every message number and NULL for unknown numbers.

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    int low = 0;
    int high = MESGS - 1;

    while (low <= high)
    {
        const int mid = (low + high) >> 1;
        const FIT_UINT16 mid_num = mesgs[mid].num;

        if (mid_num == num)
            return &mesgs[mid];
        if (mid_num < num)
            low = mid + 1;
        else
            high = mid - 1;
    }

    return NULL;
}
```